            <ArticleTitle>Disseminated cryptococcosis in an immunocompetent patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr-2016-218461</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2016-218461</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cryptococcosis is a fungal infection which is commonly associated with immune-compromised state. Disseminated infection in immunocompetent individuals is extremely rare. We present a case of a 56-year-old African American patient who presented with unilateral knee pain and swelling and was subsequently diagnosed with cryptococcal bone mass with dissemination of infection.</AbstractText>
